     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""exp_35 E5 -- descriptive only, NO verdict (plan_orbitrir_yaw_evidence.md r4 §4 E5; §14 A2: its own script, outside
     3	the runner's digest set, run after phase (ii)):
     4	
     5	1. B-F at 135 / 225 deg vs B-F at 45 deg (s42, the same pin; 135 = 45 + 90, 225 = 45 + 180): the item-weighted metric
     6	   differences (table (a)'s six metrics + FD) and the scored-dump relL2 / relLinf per item -> n, mean, median, p99, max;
     7	2. CANON at 135 / 225 deg vs CANON at 0 deg (s42): the 0-degree reference is the exp_25 T cell at d6ca307a -- a
     8	   CROSS-PIN pair, both pins recorded and disclosed;
     9	3. P1 vs angle: FLAC's mean +- sd over seeds 42-46 at 0 / 45 / 135 / 225 deg (the off-orbit figure's sources) and the
    10	   differences of the means to 0 deg, K1 and K8.
    11	
    12	Fail-closed like the figure: every figure point is verified first (``yaw_offorbit_sources.collect_points``), each pair
    13	cell the same way; items pair only on equal stream input_hash (the collector's ``make_pairs`` rule, item i with item i);
    14	each dump is verified against its receipt (``verify_cell(dump_check="manifest")``) and its bytes re-hashed against the
    15	receipt's waveform sha256 before any statistic is computed -- from exactly those bytes. Output: ``<--out>.json`` /
    16	``.md`` (default ``orbitrir_yaw_e5`` in this checkout's exp_35 folder); the md is ONE section,
    17	"## E5 (descriptive, no verdict)", for the Planner to join to the results file.
    18	
    19	Written by the exp_35 Coder (Claude Opus 5.5, max effort) for round 6b.
    20	"""
    21	import argparse
